## Step 6: WebApplicationFactory harness and initial Tier 3 smoke tests

### Status
Proposed.

### GitHub Issue
#60

### Summary
Build a full-pipeline test harness and a short list of smoke tests for behaviors only the
real HTTP pipeline exercises.

### Motivation
Authentication middleware, routing, and anti-forgery filters aren't exercised by calling
controller actions directly. This tier is deliberately small — a handful of smoke tests, not
broad coverage.

### Proposed Changes
- A `CustomWebApplicationFactory<Program>` that swaps the real database configuration for a
  SQLite in-memory `ApplicationDbContext` during tests.
- Smoke test: full create event -> join event -> sign in flow via `HttpClient`.
- Smoke test: an unauthenticated or non-Admin request to an `Areas/Admin` route is rejected.
- Smoke test: a state-changing POST without a valid anti-forgery token is rejected.

### Acceptance Criteria
- All three smoke tests pass against the real ASP.NET Core pipeline (routing, middleware,
  Identity all engaged, not bypassed).
- The factory correctly isolates its database from any other test run.

### Out of Scope
- Broad Tier 3 coverage beyond the three smoke tests listed — this tier stays intentionally
  small (see file intro).

### Dependencies
Step 1. Reuses entity builders from Step 4 where practical. Blocks Step 7's
authorization/anti-forgery tests.

---

## Step 7: Security-focused test coverage

### Status
Proposed.

### GitHub Issue
#61

### Summary
Add explicit, deliberate coverage of authorization boundaries, anti-forgery enforcement, and
input validation boundaries.

### Motivation
Security was flagged as a top priority for this test system. This step makes sure these
behaviors are explicitly covered, rather than only incidentally covered as a side effect of
the feature-focused tests in Steps 5 and 6.

### Proposed Changes
- `[Authorize(Roles="Admin")]` boundary tests for every gated action/page currently in
  `Areas/Admin` (e.g. `ManageUsers.cshtml.cs`).
- Anti-forgery token enforcement tests for all state-changing POST actions in
  `EventsController` and `MyEventsController`.
- Explicit mismatched/invalid rejoin code rejection tests in `EventsController.SignIn.cs`.
- `ModelConstants` boundary tests: max-length, min-length, and invalid-alphabet input
  rejection for display name, event code, and color fields.

### Acceptance Criteria
- Every `[Authorize]`-gated route has a test confirming unauthorized/unauthenticated
  requests are rejected.
- Every state-changing POST action has a test confirming a missing/invalid anti-forgery
  token is rejected.
- `ModelConstants` boundary tests cover both the valid-boundary and just-past-boundary cases
  for each constrained field.

### Out of Scope
- General business-logic correctness already covered in Step 5.

### Dependencies
Step 4 (SQLite harness, for validation-level tests) and Step 6 (WebApplicationFactory
harness, for authorization/anti-forgery tests requiring the real HTTP pipeline).

---

## Step 8: PostToolUse hook to auto-run affected tests

### Status
Proposed.

### GitHub Issue
#62

### Summary
Add a Claude Code `settings.json` hook that automatically re-runs the relevant test class
whenever a file under `Controllers/`, `Services/`, or `Models/` is edited.

### Motivation
The enforcement rule documented in Step 2 relies on it actually being followed every time.
This closes the loop with an automated check that surfaces regressions immediately instead
of relying on memory alone.

### Proposed Changes
- A `PostToolUse` hook in `settings.json` triggered by Edit/Write tool calls targeting paths
  under `Controllers/**`, `Services/**`, or `Models/**`.
- The hook maps the edited file to its mirrored test file/class (per the naming convention
  documented in Step 2) and runs `dotnet test` filtered to that class.
- Test results (pass/fail) surface back into the conversation without a separate manual
  `dotnet test` invocation.
- The hook is a feedback signal only — it does not block or fail the edit itself. A CI gate
  remains explicitly out of scope.

### Acceptance Criteria
- Editing a file under `Controllers/`, `Services/`, or `Models/` triggers exactly one
  `dotnet test` run filtered to the corresponding test class, with results surfaced in the
  conversation.
- The hook does not fire for edits outside those three directories.
- The hook never blocks or reverts the edit itself, regardless of test outcome.

### Out of Scope
- A CI (GitHub Actions) gate — deferred to a future, separate decision (see epic #54).
- Coverage-gap detection (i.e. flagging when a change has *no* corresponding test at all) —
  this hook only re-runs existing tests, it doesn't verify new tests were added.

### Dependencies
Step 1 (test project must exist) and Step 2 (documented naming/path convention the hook's
mapping logic relies on). This is a Claude Code harness configuration change, not
application code.
